Build a complete retro arcade Snake game in HTML/CSS/JavaScript with neon aesthetic in a single HTML file. The game offers three distinct render modes switchable via 1/2/3 keys or start-screen buttons.

**Core Gameplay:**
- **2D/2.5D:** 20×20 grid, 24px cells; **3D:** 10×10×10 volumetric cube
- Snake starts centered with 3 segments facing right; input buffer for up to 2 queued moves (prevents 180° turns and duplicates)
- Arrow keys/WASD control movement; in 3D, these are camera-relative; Q/Space rise through z-axis, E/Shift dive (real vertical moves)
- Food spawns randomly in 3D space; collision adds 1 segment, scores 10 points
- Speed: start 150ms per move, subtract 4ms per food (min 55ms); slow-mo multiplies by 1.8× when active
- Death on wall/self collision (tail safe if growing); screen shake on death (420ms decay, ±10px)

**Three Render Modes:**
- **2D:** Classic flat neon board with glowing cyan border, faint grid, snake head cyan with eyes, body fades green, food pulsing pink diamond, 32% opacity trail clearing
- **2.5D:** Same 20×20 board through fixed perspective tilt + depth shading (farther = darker); arena has glowing cyan rim, depth-sorted rendering
- **3D:** Full volumetric cube; snake lives in N×N×N space (N=10); orbitable camera (drag to rotate, scroll to zoom); wireframe cyan cage, floor shadows, pulsing ring marks current layer, elevation gauge (right side), layer readout (bottom-left); gentle auto-orbit when not dragging; depth cues: segments scale/fade with distance
- Mode selection on start screen with buttons labeled "2D / 2.5D / 3D" (no numeric prefixes); switchable anytime via 1/2/3 keys; switching 3D mid-run restarts; one persistent high score across all modes; remember last-used mode in localStorage

**Power-Ups (all modes, 3D space):**
- Yuzu Berry (yellow orb with green leaf): slow-mo (1.8×) for 6 seconds
- Ghost Star (5-point white star, cyan glow): phase through self for 6 seconds
- Spawn every 6–13 seconds, exist 9 seconds, blink when <1.5s remain; spawn randomly in free 3D cells
- Power-up HUD badges (center) with countdown timers (0.0s format), blink near expiry
- Particle bursts (14 pink/yellow particles) on grab; world-space physics with bounce

**Visual Style:**
- Dark background (#05050a); Press Start 2P font
- Neon palette: green (#39ff14), pink (#ff2ec4), cyan (#00f0ff), yellow (#ffee00)
- Ghost mode: head white, body cyan, reduced opacity with shimmer
- CRT scanlines overlay (3px dark lines) across entire page
- All modes: glowing effects via shadowBlur, depth-sorted particle/trail/entity rendering

**Effects & Audio:**
- Death animation: 650ms flashing red/white segments, descending beep (220→140→80Hz sawtooth)
- Food eat: ascending pitch beep (880Hz + min(score, 400))
- Power-up grab: ascending triple beep for star (740→990→1240 Hz), double for yuzu (520/390 Hz)
- Start: 660Hz, 880Hz beeps

**UI & States:**
- States: start, playing, paused, dying (650ms), gameover
- HUD: score (green glow, left), power badges (center), hi-score (pink glow, right); mode tag (bottom-right)
- Start screen: pulsing "NEON SNAKE" title, mode selector buttons, "INSERT COIN" button (yellow, blinking)
- Pause screen: "PAUSED" title, power-up hints, "PRESS P TO RESUME"
- Game Over: final/best scores, "NEW HI-SCORE" if applicable
- Space/Enter starts from start/game-over; arrow/WASD auto-starts; P toggles pause
